---
description: Rails 8 conventions for the sample todo app
alwaysApply: true
---

Conventions that must hold for any AI-generated change in this repo:

- Prefer Hotwire/Turbo (Turbo Streams, Turbo Frames) and Stimulus over hand-written JavaScript. No inline `<script>` in ERB.
- Use `bin/rails generate` for migrations, models, and controllers rather than hand-writing boilerplate.
- Keep all migrations reversible (`change` with reversible operations, or explicit `up`/`down`).
- Use strong parameters via the Rails 8 `params.expect(...)` style, matching the existing `TodosController`.
- Controllers respond through `respond_to` blocks; render JSON via jbuilder views (`*.json.jbuilder`), not inline `render json:` of view data.
- Tests are Minitest under `test/` — add or extend tests there. Do not introduce RSpec.
- Keep the schema scoped to this todo app. Do not import models, migrations, or tables from other projects.
- Do not add new gems or CSS frameworks (e.g. Bootstrap) without explicit approval; styling stays plain CSS under `app/assets/stylesheets/`.
